        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "1186cf68-c918-5830-8756-2d813dad0f65",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 483,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:1",
          "start": 191
        },
        "quote": "The Environmental Protection Agency, pursuant to the Federal Clean Water Act, 33 U.S.C. Section 1251 et seq., has published rules for stormwater outfall permits. The State has adopted stormwater management legislation which encourages proper management of stormwater runoff and water quality.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 13.25.010 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "c3fdd3b0-3629-50a0-9ed2-2baa48328930",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 737,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:2",
          "start": 484
        },
        "quote": "The City desires to develop a stormwater utility to be responsible for the operation, construction and maintenance of stormwater devices; for stormwater system planning and for review of development plans for compliance with stormwater management codes.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 13.25.010 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "80795760-8300-5a53-a693-218f9651a4bf",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1042,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:3",
          "start": 738
        },
        "quote": "The cost of operating and maintaining all stormwater management systems and the financing of existing and future necessary repairs, replacements, improvements, and extensions thereof, should, to the extent practicable, be allocated in relationship to the benefits enjoyed and services received therefrom.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 13.25.010 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "3dfe1f8b-683c-5280-a989-f3477e806c45",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1414,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:4",
          "start": 1043
        },
        "quote": "The City has determined that the adoption of this chapter, and the creation of a stormwater utility, under the terms, conditions and criteria set forth hereunder, is necessary to protect the health, safety and welfare of the citizens, residents and inhabitants of the City. (Ord. 19496 § 117, 12-21-10; Ord. 17059 § 13, 12-17-96. Code 1995 § 146-376. Formerly 14.85.010.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.25.010:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
